    "id": "98dbbade94b8dcc444c33b0e",
    "path": "buoyant_kernel::column_trie::ColumnTrie",
    "name": "ColumnTrie",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "buoyant_kernel",
    "version": "1.0.0+58f07cd6",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct ColumnTrie<'col>",
    "docs": "A trie (prefix tree) for efficient column path matching.\n\nThe lifetime `'col` ties this trie to the column names it was built from,\nallowing it to borrow string slices instead of cloning.\n\nThe `Default` implementation creates an empty trie node with no children and\n`is_terminal = false`. This is used both for creating a new root trie and for\ncreating intermediate nodes during insertion (via `or_default()`).",
